Every $1 invested in childhood vaccination programmes saves $10–$44 in treatment costs, hospitalisation, and lost productivity, according to CDC economic analyses.
Colorectal cancer screening via colonoscopy costs $10,000–$25,000 per quality-adjusted life year saved — far below the $100,000 threshold typically used by health systems to define 'cost-effective.'
The Diabetes Prevention Programme showed lifestyle intervention (diet + 150 min/week exercise) reduced type 2 diabetes incidence by 58% at a cost of $1,400 per case prevented, versus $13,000+ for treating established diabetes per patient per year.
